# Goldcrust Bakery — which unit sits inside which.
# Inferred from the `member-of` frontmatter of every unit (units/ and work-systems/):
# Goldcrust Bakery ⊃ three sites (Mill Lane ⊃ Deliveries, Wholesale · Market Street ·
# Station Road). The work systems carry no `member-of`: they are the flow, drawn in the
# topology, not a second time here. `layout: tree` draws the same containment as a tree.
# `focus` + `radius` scope the picture to this organization (the index spans the whole
# workspace): `up: 0` = nothing above the company root, `down: inf` = everything inside it.
mode: infer
layout: nested
focus: "[[Goldcrust Bakery]]"
radius: { up: 0, down: inf }
notes:
  - on: "[[Deliveries]]"
    text: "Second van budgeted for Q4"
